From 55e9f48af3989aa25fff60cb33653453e3c08d9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:53:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Execution policies of the backends of the generic-parallel
 interfaces

`BatchExecutionPolicy` and `AsynchronousBatchExecutionPolicy` hold a pointer
to the execution policy of the backend defined by TFEL (`backend_policy`)
instead of a `void*` queue and of the stack size flag. MGIS only forwards
this pointer: the base class of the policies is declared
(`MGIS/BackendExecutionPolicy.h`), and MGIS still builds without TFEL.

- With `AsynchronousBatchExecutionPolicy`, the computations are asynchronous
  if the backend policy requests it; otherwise they are synchronous and the
  pending computation gives the result. A backend policy requesting
  asynchronous computations is refused with `BatchExecutionPolicy`.
- `getSynchronousBatchExecutionPolicy` is removed.
- The copies of the data structures of TFEL follow its version 4
  (`statistics` and `execution_policy` members).
- The descriptions of the behaviours and of the material properties give the
  identifier of the policy expected by the library (`execution_policy`,
  `LibrariesManager::getGenericParallelExecutionPolicy`).
- Tests: the CUDA tests and the evaluation test create the policies of their
  backend and link `MFrontGenericParallelRuntime`, optional in FindTFEL.
- Documentation and release notes.
